```text
FINANCE COMMIflEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Finance Committee was held on Tuesday, April 22, 2025, in Council Chambers
and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Pete Laybourn, Chairman; Ken Esquibel; Mark Moody; and Scott
Roybal.
AGENDA ITEMS
6.
APPLICATION!LICENSESIPERMITS:
a)
Application for a bar & grill liquor license filed with the City Clerk’s Office for
Frontier Daze, LLC d/b/a Cheba Hut, 3838 Atkin St., Cheyenne, WY.
Mr. Esquibel moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Moody. Motion carried by unanimous voice
vote.
Kylie Soden, City Clerk, provided a staff report and committee member Roybal commented on
the item.
9.
ORDINANCE _3td READING - Amending Chapter 10.82, Motor-assisted Scooters,
Electric Bicycles, and Bicycles Equipped with GPS of Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, of
the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, authorizing dockless vehicle
companies to conduct business in the city using the city’s formal procurement process,
making a conforming amendment and repealing obsolete provisions.
Mr. Roybal moved to approve on 3M and final reading, seconded by Mr. Esquibel. Mr. Moody
moved to amend by striking in section 10.82.110 items Al and 8, B7, 8 and 9, and in C replacing
“one(l) or more operators” with “two(2) or more operators,” seconded by Mr. Esquibel. Motion
to amend failed with Mr. Esquibel and Mr. Roybal voting “NO” and Mr. Moody voting “YES.”
Main motion carried with Mr. Esquibel and Mr. Roybal voting “YES” and Mr. Moody voting
Charles Bloom, Planning & Development Department Director, provided a staff report and TJ
Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager, provided additional information.
All committee members
commented on the item.
10.
ORDINANCE _2MI READING - Amending and updating the Solid Waste Fee Schedule
in accordance with Section 8.44.010 of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne,
Wyoming and repealing Ordinance No.4571. (SPONSOR- ML LAYBOURN)
Mr. Roybal moved to approve on 2” reading, seconded by Mr. Esquibel. Motion carried with Mr.
Esquibel and Mr. Roybal voting “YES” and Mr. Moody voting “NO.”
```

